  "contract": {
    "operation": "In each round, select every active vertex whose priority is lower than all active neighbors, then remove those selected vertices and their active neighbors; repeat until no active vertices remain.",
    "seed": 7,
    "priority_projection": "Pannotia initializes float priorities with rand()/(float)RAND_MAX after srand(7); the portable profile supplies the distinct priority order explicitly, since C rand sequences vary by runtime. Only strict priority comparisons affect selection.",
    "source_profile": "The mis1/mis2/mis3 kernels compute active-neighbor minima, select strict local minima simultaneously, and transfer neighbor deactivations between rounds. The sequential oracle processes the same total priority order and returns the same greedy MIS.",
